# Delvers S2E08 — Golden Potato Sword

**Identity/type:** Played **Delvers Season Two Episode Eight**, archive title **Golden Potato Sword**, following [S2E07](S2E07.md). Host **says “June nineteenth, twenty twenty-one”** in the opening; this is a *spoken date*, **not independently verified publication/recording metadata**. Guest **Garrett** plays **Marsh**, a silver-ranked wood-elf dragon hunter. **Opening GM bridge** establishes that the Delvers **have delivered living captive Ambermoor to guild holding cells, under Zone of Truth oversight, offscreen between episodes**, and Cassius immediately sent them to help Marsh; the handoff is **not newly played in a debrief scene**. This resolves but must not erase S2E07's earlier cutoff at Krandal's farm.

**Actual end of S2E08:** **Red dragon alive**, active fight **unfinished** in the **Chath/Chaff Peak** mountaintop lair. Dragon is flying, its breath has recharged, **Koh has pressed lava-off** flooding room with sight-blocking steam, **gate-seal and forced-landing controls not yet triggered**. Guest and cast agree to continue the encounter next episode. No dragon slaying, guild payout, captured hoard, quest completion, or return journey played.

**Evidence, 2026-10-25 — ASR-provisional.** Read **all primary Parakeet spoken source-clock windows from 00:00 through 02:56:46.070/outro**; entire Qwen-labelled export parsed for exact ordered word comparison, with **selected independent Qwen semantic windows** ~00–09, 13–20, 39–47, 61–69, 82–94, 111–118, 121–133, 143–151, 156–165, 169–177 minutes, **not a second complete narrative pass**. No listening to original MP3, timeline alignment, episode publisher check, original Discord GM encounter/map or player-sheet artifact confirmation. Current **local MCP checkout clean at HEAD `14c70f8be6772f0f7c7bd3e53fb8301da01e80d5`**. GitHub reader **cannot resolve that commit**, so remote default-branch **content blobs below** were used for complete-export parsing and editorial reading; local MCP **opening and terminal SRT lines/cue counts/end clocks match**, but **byte-for-byte whole-file workspace/remote equivalence was not established**. Thus preserve *separate* revision and source-provenance limitation; do not imply the remote SHA is a local checkout hash. [ASR report](../../reports/DELVERS_S2E08_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md) · [Review queue](../REVIEW_QUEUE.md).

