## Episode evidence, chronological source clock

| Approx. SRT clock | Played action or attributed information |
| --- | --- |
| **00:00–00:10** | Host date/cast and guild opening. GM retrospective says **Ambermoor brought to guild holding cells offscreen**, Cassius promptly assigned Delvers to escort **new guest Marsh** on `Dragon Mountain`. Marsh **actually enters guild, chooses Chath Peak quest and speaks with dwarf clerk**. Tall adult **wood elf**, salt-and-pepper hair, **left facial chemical-like burn scar, partly missing left ear**, practical coat/cowboy-or-farm hat, **dragon-bone bow and dagger hilts** and silver badge. Guild advertises **young red dragon (~100 years)**, **1,000 gp quest reward / 250 per four members**, **treasure hoard may be split by negotiation**, **no reward yet**. Clerk says last dragon there ~150 years ago was **green** and killed by **Radiant Lance** (former dragon's name `Banny Ruba` ASR provisional). Marsh takes guild horse and rides ~3 hours to Aegis's cart; party is already at mountain road. |
| **~00:10–00:25** | Party meets Marsh: **Koh** purple concealing Sultan's Sash, **Evelyn** short ~18 with hair buns/hammer/javelins, **Krandal** large half-orc with holy symbol and face maces, eating raw potato. Aegis gives **guild fire-resistance armor replacements**: two **studded leathers for Koh and Marsh**, **chain for Evelyn**, **scale for Krandal** (with reflection strips on metal suits); attunement/equipping discussed. **Krandal temporarily unattunes Staff of the Python, kept in Evelyn's Bag of Holding**, to make attunement room; **Marsh replaces his acid-resistant armor** for fire protection. Guild horse leaves with Aegis, cart collection promised near dusk, not yet performed. Marsh has a **dark weasel familiar/companion Wheatley (Wheatly?)**, scruffy face “mask”; relationship familiar vs pet not established mechanically. |
| **~00:25–00:40** | Marsh leads game trail toward **Chath/Chaff Peak**, silver adventurer instructs bronze **Darkest Delvers**. Spots **kobold tracks**; party sees distant flying red dragon. After ~2h they reach **waterfall**, several kobolds hauling water in basin ~120 ft below; avoid fighting them and prepare ropes/pitons plus **Sultan's Sash** to traverse ~3-foot ledge behind falls. Krandal's noisy maces impose poor stealth; **Marsh leads**, then Koh, Evelyn, Krandal last. |
| **~00:40–01:03** | **Enormous red dragon lands at water below**, **Marsh estimates ~450 years old**, contradicting clerk's ~100-year expectation; age is **Marsh expert estimate**, not dated biological confirmation. **Koh, Evelyn and Krandal fail Frightful Presence**; Marsh unaffected. Wheatley and Koh's **Psychic Whispers** aid attempts to rally them; **Krandal casts Shield of Faith while panicked**, uses Staff of Python's **carved head to obscure Evelyn's view**, then **carries Evelyn behind waterfall**, releasing her after recovery. Marsh urges battle in **lair rather than open air**, to prevent escaping flyer. At exit, Krandal's clanging maces expose them; dragon flies over cliff and attacks group with fire breath: **56 raw fire, 28 to failing wearers with fire resistance, 14 to successful Evelyn** (individual roll details in sources). **Not a fight to dragon death**; dragon flies off. |
| **~01:03–01:17** | After breath, **Krandal casts Cure Wounds twice on Koh**, **Evelyn lays on 20 points healing to Marsh** (described as her healing slap); exact other HP recovery not extrapolated. **Krandal stores noisy face maces in Evelyn's Bag of Holding** for stealth; Shield of Faith still visually glimmers as discussed. Later ascending the mountain they see **kobold village holding revel** and watch **three tied kobolds on a long log** carried to edge as **living offerings**, red dragon carries beam away, later seen **eating last captive**. No rescue attempt. |
| **~01:17–01:38** | At break return **Skoogie/Scoogy (ASR variant)**, flamboyantly feather-hatted **kobold shaman** with bell and caged lizard, approaches and speaks **Draconic** understood by Marsh only (who translates to party). Skoogie says dragon came **~a month ago**, usurped shaman's followers; **asks party to kill dragon and leave kobold community to Skoogie**. Credibility and binding status of later joking foot-massage bargaining unproven. Offers secret lair route and **actual Arrow of Dragon Slaying**, hidden as feathered pole atop hat, **given to Marsh**. Party takes **short rest** (GM offers). Skoogie joins/escorts with bell; **not an enemy**. |
| **~01:38–01:56** | Lava stream crossing: Marsh casts **Jump**, crosses via stepping rocks; Koh attempts Mirthful Leaps with Guidance, reaches first stone but **takes 5 fire after resistance**; Krandal crosses with Guidance and **casts Create/Destroy Water to cool/solidify flowing lava**, producing short-lived moving foothold. Evelyn carries Skoogie piggyback across, rest jump to Marsh. Marsh spots dragon **eating third kobold** and **slit/crag scratched by dragon claws**; party enters concealed lava-tube passage rather than challenging dragon in sky. |
| **~01:56–02:17** | Ancient **obsidian stone chamber**, pipes and pedestal with **3D miniature of upcoming lair**. Attributed ancient-elvish inscription **signed Radiant Lance** instructs would-be dragon slayer to prove **freedom from greed**. Color-coded controls noted: **red: Lava Off**, **blue: Sealed Gate**, **green: Forced Landing**. These are **actual labels/working mechanism leads**, not proof all switches activated. **Evelyn places ALL on-hand ~250 gp into trough; Krandal adds half-eaten potato**, Evelyn uses wall handprint. Mechanism **actually consumes gold**, potato **burns away**, fashions and gives Evelyn a **Dragon Slayer's Longsword**; title/properties per GM, against dragon later uses extra damage. **No golden potato fused into hilt**; name is episode joke. |
| **~02:17–02:25** | Koh tries **1,000 ball bearings**, uses deceptive intent/psionic check; receives only crude fused-metal lump. Krandal tries **candles (includes interest in Candle of the Deep)** under a selfless pretense; molten wax splashes/clogs machinery, **no upgraded candle, sword or magic benefit**. Marsh **does not attempt** forge. Model-within-model center activates lift; all including Skoogie step onto **rising platform**. Marsh drinks **Potion of Fire Resistance** (fire-armor stack not adjudicated separately). Koh prepares his sash as lasso; Krandal casts **Guidance on Marsh** for initiative, but do not infer its duration beyond GM rolls. |
| **~02:25–02:43** | Platform rises to actual dragon **lair in Chath Peak**: broad **moat of lava**, bridges, walkways and ramps leading 20 ft then **40-ft high dragon perch**, sizeable gold hoard **and wagon with skeletal horses**. Control **Lava Off (north), Sealed Gate (east), Forced Landing (south)**. Red dragon speaks and mocks party and sword; **Skoogie gives all temporary 10 HP** by bell magic; **GM inspiration granted**. **Krandal actually casts Aid at level 3, adding 10 to maximum and current HP** (distinct from temp HP). This is a **played combat**, not merely planning. |
| **~02:43–02:50** | Dragon **first lair breath** and flight: **28 fire damage for failed saves with resistance, 14 on success**, largely mitigated by armor and temporary HP. **Koh double-dashes to north lava-off button**, not yet presses; **Marsh casts Jump and moves toward east gate-seal**. **Skoogie is set alight/collapses**, **Evelyn actually heals Skoogie by 3**, and runs toward forced-landing button. Krandal **summons Spiritual Weapon but dragon at 80 ft is out of 60-ft reach**, moves toward ramp. Dragon's flyby **bites Marsh (17 damage)**; Marsh **opportunity dagger hit**; dragon claw attacks Evelyn miss and **Evelyn's opportunity swing with new dragon-slayer sword (inspiration reroll to natural 20, not double critical)** deals **~37 adjudicated damage**. Dragon **NOT killed**. |
| **~02:50–02:56:46** | **Koh actually activates Lava Off**: water jets hit lava, generating **thick steam that heavily obscures the battlefield**. Koh draws and coats **Dagger of Venom** then moves away from threatened spot; **Marsh casts Pass Without Trace and continues toward the gate-seal control, not yet activates it**. **Skoogie gives Evelyn a lightstone**, Evelyn casts **Locate Object to navigate toward Forced Landing but does not trigger button**. **Krandal casts Create/Destroy Water to disperse local ~40-ft steam area** (spell effect performed), moves **into wagon atop dragon's hoard for cover without taking gold**. Dragon **breathes again into Koh's vacated area through remaining steam**, no recorded second-breath damage to him at this moment. **Koh moves toward wall and begins a stealth maneuver**, exact success not completed before GM/cast **stop the episode mid-encounter** due to guest scheduling. **No killed dragon, hoard payout, return to guild, final button activation or completion of contract**. Host says **Garrett will return next episode to continue**, a production plan, not played outcome. |

## Character/item custody and open continuity at cutoff

- **Guest Marsh:** wood elf / silver-ranked dragon slayer at Chath Peak, **dragon-bone bow/dagger hilts, scarred left face and partly missing left ear, cowboy-like farm hat and weasel Wheatley**. **Receives Arrow of Dragon Slaying from Skoogie**; no confirmed arrow **fired** before cutoff. **Wearing guild fire-resistant studded leather rather than original acid resistance suit**, potion of fire resistance **drunk**; **Pass Without Trace cast** in final lair, **not proven effective against steam or dragon**. He is pursuing **east gate-seal control**, **not activated**.
- **Evelyn:** holds forged **Dragon Slayer's Longsword** made from her ~250 gp **actually sacrificed** (half potato burnt, no potato-sword composite); wearing guild fire suppression **chain armor**; sword **hits dragon in opportunity attack**. **Skoogie heals 3 via Evelyn**, she later **receives lightstone**, heads south with Locate Object toward **Forced Landing** but does not press it. Her Bag of Holding currently **holds Krandal's face maces during trek**, he retrieves them near battle; **Staff of Python kept in bag, still temporarily unattuned**.
- **Koh:** wearing guild fire resistant **studded leather** in place of Glamoured Studded Leather (prior item still owned, not destroyed). **Sultan's Sash** deployed as fall-prevention rope then wound up; preps lasso before lair. Finds mechanisms and **presses north Lava Off**, producing steam. **Dagger of Venom poison readied**, no verified hit; sneaks/moves in fog toward wall as episode stops. Failed forge test with 1,000 ball bearings produces **lumpy metal, not effective sword**; exact retention unspecified.
- **Krandal:** fire resistant **scale armor** replacing normal, temporarily **unattunes Staff of Python** to make attunement space (not lost); face maces stowed in Evelyn bag while traversing, recovered at beginning of dragon battle. Casts **Aid (level 3, +10 max/current HP)** and **Spiritual Weapon**, failed reach when dragon high, then **Create/Destroy Water to clear part of steam**; is in **treasure wagon for cover**, **no looting or sword received**. Half potato burnt in forge; candles melted and may impair mechanism.
- **Skoogie:** helper kobold shaman, gives Marsh arrow, bell **10 temporary HP per party member**, burned by dragon breath yet **revived/healed 3 by Evelyn**. No death confirmed at cutoff. **Guest Wheatley** not given to shaman, no harm shown.
- **Earlier Gemholm:** S2E07 **ends** at farm with restrained Ambermoor; S2E08 GM establishes **offscreen subsequent handoff to guild under Zone of Truth** before taking Dragon Mountain assignment. **No transcript scene of formal inquiry, reward or cure of two still-missing slaadi**. Experimental reagent briefcase's exact transfer in intervening handoff is **NOT stated**, so do not claim Cassius took the colored vials.
- **Review priorities:** Guest proper name and spelling **Marsh/Wheatley**, **Chath/Chaff Peak**, kobold **Skoogie**, former dragon **Banny Ruba**, Radiant Lance old inscriptions, **dragon age 450 vs guild 100 estimate**, true name/level of sword and arrow, actual armor item names/attunements, exact fire-breath saves and HP, duration of steam/Pass Without Trace, whether **Sealed Gate** and **Forced Landing** remain untouched (yes at present), meaning of powered lair machinery and the potion's resistance stacking. **Actual GM map and item link posted on Discord not inspected**; canonical details remain provisional.

